# Fixed defect 133, 2026-09-29. Symptom: inside an `extern` group, `struct
# Pair` over a field missing its colon cost `reserved_word` and then
# `expected_extern_signature` at the field block, which the group took for
# a member of its own; only once `check --apply` had written `record Pair`
# was the field's own mistake, `expected_field_type`, reported. An `extern`
# with no members above a `fn` line was silent the same way. Cause: the
# lexer emits the refused word as an `error` token, and the group's member
# loop recovered past it. A member opened by `fn`, `func`, `const` or
# `struct` is now read as the `function`, `constant` or `record` its
# certain swap writes (`parse/swap_reading.hero`). `enum` writes `variant`,
# which no group holds, so it is read as nothing there and costs the word
# alone. An empty group is refused at the next line's first token, as it
# is after the swap.

extern "math.h"
    function sqrt(x: f64) -> f64  #~ reserved_word
    constant M_PI: f64  #~ reserved_word
    record Pair  #~ reserved_word
        a i32  #~ expected_field_type
    variant Mode  #~ reserved_word
    function cbrt(x: f64) f64  #~ reserved_word expected_extern_signature
    function floor(x: f64) -> f64

extern "stdio.h"

function main()  #~ reserved_word expected_extern_block
    print(1)
